WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.962
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.962 --> 00:08.302
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.302 --> 00:11.930
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.055 --> 00:14.975
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.058 --> 00:18.185
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.311 --> 00:23.110
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.194 --> 00:24.861
"Laugh and cry

00:24.987 --> 00:30.201
"He's a family guy

00:34.457 --> 00:38.420
Look, I'm that pretty dark-haired
figure skater with the horse teeth,

00:38.545 --> 00:40.839
the one who got what she had coming.

00:40.922 --> 00:43.343
Nice figure eight, Mom.

00:50.100 --> 00:52.312
Ha! All right!

00:52.395 --> 00:55.230
OK, Bonnie. One, two, three, push!

00:57.815 --> 01:00.238
Oh! Ah! Whoa!

01:04.200 --> 01:07.536
My God! I can walk! It's a mira...!

01:08.663 --> 01:10.874
- Sorry, Dad.
- Just get the chair.

01:14.505 --> 01:17.633
Good shot.
Made my brown eye blue with that one.

01:17.759 --> 01:22.346
- Yeah. Next one's coming for your head!
- Oh, no! No, help! Oh, help!

01:23.263 --> 01:26.519
- What the hell?
- Now is the winter of your discontent!

01:28.811 --> 01:30.898
You wanna race? On your mark, get set, go!

01:30.982 --> 01:33.819
First to where
that Pakistani girl fell through the ice

01:33.902 --> 01:36.737
after coming to the States
for her severely burned face

01:36.821 --> 01:41.202
she got when the man she refused to marry
dumped sulphuric acid on her, wins. I win!

01:41.327 --> 01:44.873
Yes! Yes! In your face! In your face!

01:44.956 --> 01:47.585
In my face! In my face!

01:48.418 --> 01:52.259
Ahh! No! Acid girl! It's acid girl! Ahh!

01:57.597 --> 01:59.974
- James Woods High! Whoo!
- Hey, guys.

02:00.100 --> 02:03.019
- What do you want?
- I'm trying out for cheerleading.

02:03.102 --> 02:06.858
Peter Rabbit would be wise
to stay out of Mr McGregor's garden.

02:06.984 --> 02:10.111
Why don't you try the flag girls squad?

02:15.534 --> 02:17.498
Are you trying out for flag girl?

02:25.338 --> 02:27.299
Yes! I win again, Andy.

02:27.425 --> 02:31.389
One more before
the missus notices I'm not on the couch.

02:31.389 --> 02:33.681
Too late!

02:37.020 --> 02:40.565
Hey, careful, Quagmire.
Don't get too close to that thing.

02:42.233 --> 02:43.986
Did I just get laid?

02:44.111 --> 02:46.404
- Nice game, Peter.
- I'm on a roll.

02:46.487 --> 02:50.034
- I whipped Chris on the ice today.
- Enjoy it while it lasts.

02:50.159 --> 02:52.746
It's only a matter of time
before he beats you.

02:52.870 --> 02:58.086
What? I'm better than him at everything:
Sports, video games, even magic tricks.

02:59.753 --> 03:04.134
- Ha-ha. Got your nose.
- Oh, yeah? Well, I got your face.

03:07.763 --> 03:10.892
Calm down, Chris. It's only a trick.

03:11.017 --> 03:14.147
Face it, sooner or later
you'll have to pass the torch.

03:14.230 --> 03:17.692
I remember the first time
Kevin beat me. I was so proud,

03:17.775 --> 03:21.737
I gave him a little congratulatory
punch in the arm. Then another.

03:21.865 --> 03:26.246
Then everything got hazy. Kevin went
to live with a foster family for a while...

03:26.329 --> 03:28.538
- It's inevitable.
- Don't feel bad.

03:28.622 --> 03:30.833
I think I know why your son beat you.

03:30.916 --> 03:34.797
Apparently, you're
a 12-year-old prepubescent girl.

03:34.881 --> 03:40.512
Which is good, cos I finally have someone
to give this training bra to. Here, Josephina.

03:40.636 --> 03:43.014
Does it feel good
on your new budding bosoms?

03:43.140 --> 03:46.267
- It sure does...
- Get the hell off me!

03:48.354 --> 03:51.567
Rudolph, we figured out
what makes your nose red.

03:51.692 --> 03:55.446
- Is it pixie dust or leprechaun tails?
- No, it's a tumour.

03:55.530 --> 03:58.031
You mean like
a magical Christmas tumour?

03:58.156 --> 04:02.414
No, a malignant tumour, the base of which
is lodged deep within your brain.

04:02.539 --> 04:07.628
- Oh. Like a happy special...
- You're going to die.

04:08.169 --> 04:10.463
Hey, everybody, guess what I am.

04:10.546 --> 04:14.846
The end result of a drunken backseat
gropefest and a broken prophylactic?

04:14.929 --> 04:19.433
- I'm on the flag girl squad!
- Oh, honey, congratulations.

04:19.516 --> 04:23.604
- Hey, Chris. I bet you can't do this.
- I bet I can!

04:23.687 --> 04:27.443
We perform at all the football games.
I'm practically a cheerleader!

04:27.568 --> 04:30.571
That's wonderful. Isn't that wonderful?

04:30.697 --> 04:35.367
Way to go, Stewie. Chris, I'll see
your fork and raise you a gravy ladle.

04:35.492 --> 04:36.536
You're on!

04:36.620 --> 04:39.458
So, you're a flag girl. That's great, Meg.

04:39.541 --> 04:41.959
Yes, yes.

04:42.043 --> 04:46.005
Now you can be somewhere else
when the boys don't call.

04:47.674 --> 04:51.553
- All right. Salt shaker up the nose.
- I got pepper.

04:53.307 --> 04:55.935
Ha-ha! Yes! I win!

04:56.018 --> 04:58.104
- That was fun, Dad!
- I'm the man!

04:58.229 --> 05:00.940
Yeah! Ahh!

05:01.023 --> 05:07.282
Lois, go get the medical dictionary
and look up "fork" and "lung. "

05:07.407 --> 05:09.577
- Why?
- Time's a factor, Lois.

05:14.916 --> 05:19.088
Say, Meg, looking sharp.
You want to go out after the game tonight?

05:19.088 --> 05:22.717
Neil, I'm a flag girl now.
I'm way too cool to be seen with you.

05:22.842 --> 05:27.514
Really? Not even
if I smoke this corncob pipe?

05:36.608 --> 05:39.403
Are we all ready to cheer
at the game tonight?

05:39.527 --> 05:42.865
"We?" Oh, you made flag girl, huh?

05:42.948 --> 05:46.203
Yeah. This morning my mom
was, like, "Don't forget your lunch",

05:46.286 --> 05:49.542
and I'm all "I'm a flag girl now,
I won't forget my lunch",

05:49.625 --> 05:52.669
and she's all
"Don't forget your halftime routine. "

05:52.669 --> 05:57.344
Moms! Hey, maybe we could all,
like, hang out after the game.

05:57.469 --> 05:59.552
Go, team!

05:59.970 --> 06:02.056
Uncool people are like animals.

06:02.139 --> 06:05.059
You want to go feed
the science club after school?

06:14.446 --> 06:16.531
Look at me.

06:17.156 --> 06:21.535
Look at me, I'm smoking.
Dog, dog, look, look...

06:21.660 --> 06:25.834
Alcohol doesn't really make you warmer.
It constricts the blood vessels...

06:25.917 --> 06:28.754
- Shut up.
- The dog just told me to shut up.

06:28.837 --> 06:31.882
I demand to know
what you plan to do about this. Hey!

06:31.882 --> 06:35.426
- Hey! The dog just told me...
- Be quiet, Stewie.

06:37.515 --> 06:40.642
- Freezing my nips off out here.
- Oh, look, there's Meg.

06:40.726 --> 06:44.814
Meg! Meg! Meg!

06:47.943 --> 06:50.113
- Hi, Meg.
- Hi, Meg.

06:50.239 --> 06:52.323
Here we go.

07:04.505 --> 07:08.051
- Isn't she beautiful?
- Yeah, but I think she's with that guy.

07:08.175 --> 07:10.971
- They've held hands all night.
- I mean Meg.

07:11.096 --> 07:13.807
Oh. Oh, yeah. Yeah, she's hot.

07:16.102 --> 07:21.192
- Oh! This meat stinks something fierce!
- This'll knock her down a couple notches.

07:31.120 --> 07:35.999
Yea, Meg! Oh, man, I love how
these kids celebrate these days!

07:39.463 --> 07:44.261
What do you got? What do you got?
Huh? Huh? Come on.

07:44.344 --> 07:48.015
- Come on, ref. That's charging.
- Your feet were moving. No foul.

07:48.098 --> 07:52.478
No foul?! Oh, that's a stupid call!
And I know something about stupid calls.

07:54.566 --> 07:55.608
Hello?

07:55.733 --> 08:00.822
I can't take out the garbage. I'm at
the office and they're making me stay late.

08:00.947 --> 08:03.533
Caller ID says you're
calling from the kitchen.

08:03.658 --> 08:07.205
- In fact, I can see you.
- Can you see me now?

08:07.288 --> 08:09.082
- No.
- Now I'm at the office.

08:09.165 --> 08:13.253
Score's tied, next basket wins.
You might finally beat your old man.

08:13.335 --> 08:16.047
"Old man"? I'm the white Larry Bird.

08:16.172 --> 08:19.303
What do you got?
What do you got? Huh? Come on!

08:19.303 --> 08:23.056
- Your mother and I are getting a divorce!
- You are?

08:23.056 --> 08:26.060
Yes! Yes! Oh, no, we worked it out.

08:26.186 --> 08:27.519
Yes!

08:28.063 --> 08:31.398
Son, you played good,
but your dad is still number one.

08:31.481 --> 08:37.324
- Yeah, I don't think I'll ever beat you.
- Hey, Chris, what's with your leg?

08:37.449 --> 08:39.952
Oh, my God! That's not your leg!

08:49.213 --> 08:51.632
- What's wrong, honey?
- I'll tell you:

08:51.632 --> 08:54.219
I try to make love to you
and you think about Chris.

08:54.344 --> 08:58.934
- Is there something you need to tell me?
- Thanks to you, our son has a huge wang.

08:58.934 --> 09:01.645
- Thanks to me?
- He didn't get it from me.

09:01.728 --> 09:04.565
- What are you talking about?
- I'll show you.

09:07.151 --> 09:09.236
All right, stand back, Lois.

09:09.362 --> 09:12.367
Oh, my. No wonder he's always slouching.

09:12.492 --> 09:15.703
How did this happen?
I'm supposed to be the man of the house.

09:15.828 --> 09:18.122
- You must be ashamed of me.
- Oh, Peter.

09:18.205 --> 09:22.501
I care as much about the size of your penis
as you care about the size of my breasts.

09:22.586 --> 09:24.673
Oh, my God!

09:27.926 --> 09:30.513
You can't let those awful kids get to you.

09:30.638 --> 09:33.974
They won't. I'm never
going back to that school again.

09:34.058 --> 09:39.398
- Dad, could you help me with my algebra?
- You're a big man. You figure it out.

09:39.482 --> 09:43.361
I bet there's a part of you
that wants to be friends with them.

09:43.361 --> 09:45.656
- Maybe.
- So be nice to them.

09:45.739 --> 09:48.576
Win your enemies over
with unflappable kindness.

09:48.659 --> 09:52.955
- Chris, drink your milk. It'll make you big.
- No! No more milk for him.

09:53.039 --> 09:55.458
He's had enough. Give me that.

09:56.168 --> 10:01.297
Megan, you must try the brisket. I'll serve it
in the manner to which you're accustomed.

10:01.297 --> 10:02.635
Oh!

10:02.760 --> 10:07.765
Come talk to me sometime, sweetheart.
I know what it takes to be cool.

11:37.331 --> 11:40.376
Oh, yeah. That's the good stuff.

11:45.255 --> 11:47.760
- Hi, you guys.
- God, it's her.

11:48.302 --> 11:52.056
- Look, about the other night...
- Oh, that was hilarious.

11:52.056 --> 11:56.435
I just wish I'd known ahead of time.
I would've brought potato salad!

11:57.687 --> 12:00.275
You guys want tomorrow's biology test?

12:00.400 --> 12:03.820
- Whoa! How'd you get that?
- I spent the night with Mr Burler.

12:09.576 --> 12:13.833
Ah, the sun's up.
I'm safe for another night. Thanks, Meg.

12:13.958 --> 12:16.753
- Wow, thanks!
- See ya.

12:16.878 --> 12:19.589
- That was kinda cool.
- Yeah.

12:19.589 --> 12:20.632
I'm bored.

12:20.715 --> 12:23.968
Wanna go push the janitor,
knowing he can't legally push us back?

12:23.968 --> 12:26.889
- Sure!
- OK, cool. Let's go do it.

12:29.809 --> 12:33.772
Hey, Dad. Look at these little bananas.

12:33.855 --> 12:35.940
Why, you smug little bastard!

12:36.066 --> 12:41.281
Peter! Chris, these are plantains.
And there's nothing wrong with them.

12:41.365 --> 12:45.536
In fact, a lot of women prefer them
to normal-size bananas,

12:45.661 --> 12:50.878
because they're exotic and flavourful
and very, very special.

12:50.961 --> 12:56.800
Sure, all the sorority girls are clamouring
for the plantain section. Stop with this!

12:56.926 --> 12:59.428
You're overreacting to this Chris stuff.

12:59.511 --> 13:03.389
I mean, mine goes inside me
when I stand up. How do you think I feel?

13:03.475 --> 13:06.521
- Is Dad mad at me?
- Oh, of course not, honey.

13:06.605 --> 13:11.192
Go pick out a box of cereal and meet me
at the ten-inches-or-less line. Items!

13:12.778 --> 13:17.576
Nice, huh? Huh? Yeah. You like this?

13:18.202 --> 13:22.581
Stop it, Peter. You're embarrassing me.
Look, I know you're upset, but...

13:22.665 --> 13:26.335
- Oh, my God. Where's Stewie?
- He's around.

13:26.335 --> 13:29.045
Let me out of this
stink-filled corduroy dungeon!

13:29.045 --> 13:32.675
- Peter, that's sick!
- It's OK. He's outside the underwear.

13:34.761 --> 13:38.641
- Enjoy your new car, Mr Griffin.
- Thanks, Jim.

13:47.402 --> 13:53.742
When you pull that thing into your garage,
does the garage say "Is it in yet?"

13:59.501 --> 14:02.002
Don't worry, baby. I'll be gentle.

14:17.854 --> 14:20.022
Ow. My pride.

14:21.610 --> 14:25.365
You were right. I was nice to the cool kids
and they didn't spit on me.

14:25.365 --> 14:28.158
Connie Demico even
invited me to her sweet 16.

14:28.283 --> 14:31.830
Wonderful! What time do we nail
those snot-nosed punks?!

14:31.913 --> 14:35.252
Nail them? You told me
to win them over with kindness.

14:35.377 --> 14:40.466
Yes. Now that they think you're their friend,
it's the perfect time to exact your revenge.

14:40.591 --> 14:41.633
Revenge?

14:41.716 --> 14:45.678
I'm like one of those bald eagles
you see on the Discovery Channel:

14:45.804 --> 14:48.726
Beautiful to look at,
but mess with one of my chicks

14:48.726 --> 14:53.314
and I'll use my razor-sharp talons to rip
your eyes out! Cookies are done.

14:53.397 --> 14:55.817
- Who wants chocolate-chip?
- I do!

14:55.901 --> 15:00.491
But keep talking. All this stuff about
eye-gouging has gotten me all frisky.

15:00.823 --> 15:03.952
Really. I've got about half a pack
of Rolaids in my diaper.

15:10.834 --> 15:14.174
I'm glad you want to join
the National Gun Association.

15:14.257 --> 15:17.718
Let me show you around.
This is our shooting range.

15:27.938 --> 15:31.484
Here we have our locker room
with full shower facilities.

15:31.985 --> 15:35.114
Holy crap! They're all so... small!

15:35.239 --> 15:39.829
You see, Peter, the way we look at it,
a man's only as big as the gun he carries.

15:39.912 --> 15:43.374
Sign me up, and get me
the biggest freakin' gun you got!

15:43.458 --> 15:48.587
- Stewie, you can come out now.
- Turn off the light. I'm reading a ghost story.

15:53.178 --> 15:54.637
Pull!

15:55.054 --> 15:58.475
Oh, yeah.
Who's the big man now, huh?

15:58.600 --> 16:01.103
- Madonna or Janet Jackson?
- Which Janet?

16:01.186 --> 16:04.442
- Velvet Rope.
- Yeah, that one. Pull!

16:04.442 --> 16:08.612
- What the hell are you doing with that?
- You want to touch it? Go on.

16:08.612 --> 16:12.241
Careful. We don't want it to get
too excited and go off in your hand.

16:12.366 --> 16:15.912
This is pathetic. All because
you feel inadequate next to Chris.

16:15.912 --> 16:20.377
Don't be stupid. I don't need to compete
with my son or his freakishly large penis.

16:20.502 --> 16:23.420
- I'm a freak.
- Don't despair.

16:23.420 --> 16:27.676
Let's hang a tyre on the end of it
and head on down to the ol' swimming hole.

16:28.927 --> 16:34.143
Connie Demico's house is two storeys.
If we set up booby traps here, here...

16:34.268 --> 16:38.106
- How'd you get these blueprints?
- Oh, your mother has her ways.

16:38.231 --> 16:40.525
She has her ways.

16:40.525 --> 16:43.531
- Can I have those blueprints?
- Sure, here you go.

16:43.656 --> 16:47.826
Now I've put together
a little flash bomb to create a diversion.

16:47.910 --> 16:50.537
I used to date
the pyro guy from Whitesnake.

16:50.620 --> 16:51.788
What's Whitesnake?

16:51.788 --> 16:56.795
That's the music mommies and daddies
listen to. Fire in the hole!

16:59.173 --> 17:02.218
Some guys from the club
are going hunting tomorrow.

17:02.218 --> 17:04.095
- Count me in.
- Hunting?

17:04.179 --> 17:07.640
- You were gonna play hockey with Chris.
- Bring him along.

17:07.640 --> 17:10.978
- Oh, no. It's too dangerous.
- Lois, Lois.

17:10.978 --> 17:15.859
The National Gun Association is all about
safety, especially when it comes to kids.

17:15.984 --> 17:18.153
Take a look at our new video.

17:22.034 --> 17:25.871
Let's face it, your kids will get
into your guns. That's a fact.

17:25.995 --> 17:30.166
Gun accidents can be avoided by
introducing your children to guns early.

17:30.250 --> 17:34.755
Hi! I'm Petey the pistol.
Say, do you ever get lonely?

17:34.755 --> 17:38.302
- Yes.
- Me, too. Hold me.

17:38.385 --> 17:41.515
If you squeeze me,
I make bad people go away.

17:41.639 --> 17:44.852
But wait a minute.
I thought guns were bad.

17:44.977 --> 17:46.854
False! Guns are good.

17:46.937 --> 17:51.651
In fact, did you know that Jesus and Moses
used guns to conquer the Romans?

17:53.529 --> 17:57.574
So remember: Guns don't kill people,
dangerous minorities do.

18:02.166 --> 18:04.667
See, Lois? They're responsible.

18:09.589 --> 18:13.846
Hey. Hey, check it out, Chris.
I can write my name in the snow.

18:15.222 --> 18:18.351
- This is fun, Dad.
- Son, son, I told you.

18:18.435 --> 18:21.896
Out here in the wilderness,
call me Rooster Cogburn.

18:21.979 --> 18:25.316
I was starting to think
you didn't like me any more.

18:25.441 --> 18:29.823
Shh. Chris, look! Tracks.
There must be a deer around here.

18:29.823 --> 18:33.034
- Those are snowmobile tracks.
- Shh! There he is.

18:40.544 --> 18:44.423
Such grace. That's the thing
about hunting - you gotta be patient.

18:45.675 --> 18:47.760
What the hell was that?!

18:57.021 --> 19:00.566
Put this in the heating grate
and set it off in five minutes.

19:00.691 --> 19:02.778
I changed my mind. I won't do it.

19:02.778 --> 19:05.991
- They're my friends now.
- They pelted you with meat.

19:06.116 --> 19:09.953
Did you forget the neighbour kids
chased you and sprinkled you with fixings?

19:10.078 --> 19:12.663
Yes, I did!

19:12.790 --> 19:16.001
OK. Now we're gonna play
Seven Minutes in Heaven,

19:16.126 --> 19:21.633
and it's my party, so I want Doug
to go in the closet with... Meg.

19:23.928 --> 19:26.013
Have fun.

19:28.642 --> 19:33.108
OK. Everyone get ready.
Say hello to the lovers.

19:38.028 --> 19:41.364
I don't know who should be
more humiliated, Meg or the pig.

19:41.448 --> 19:44.497
- She's such a dork.
- I think I feel worse for the pig.

19:46.163 --> 19:50.127
Mom, you were right!
I should have just stuck to the plan!

19:50.127 --> 19:55.756
I figured you might get soft on me,
so I hired an old friend to scar them for life.

19:58.054 --> 20:00.555
- Hey there, sweetie. How old are you?
- 16.

20:00.640 --> 20:03.266
- 18?! You're first.
- Mom!

20:03.266 --> 20:07.313
I like where this is going.
Giggidy-giggidy-good-goody.

20:08.063 --> 20:11.904
Don't worry, Chris, I'll handle the bear.
Say hello to Satan for me!

20:15.865 --> 20:17.741
It's a boy, Mrs Griffin.

20:17.868 --> 20:21.413
I'm afraid the fever
has affected his motor skills.

20:21.413 --> 20:24.210
He's gonna have to repeat the fourth grade.

20:24.335 --> 20:28.089
Looks like he'll have to repeat
the fourth grade, Mrs Griffin.

20:28.173 --> 20:32.469
The only way to get rid of them
is with this shampoo and a tiny comb.

20:32.469 --> 20:35.596
Congratulations.
You've passed the fourth grade.

20:35.596 --> 20:39.144
Great. I gotta leave though.
I'm going hunting with my son.

20:39.769 --> 20:43.940
Dad, I know what to do!
I saw it on Fox's When Bears Attack!

20:44.023 --> 20:50.198
Go away! Go on, get!
Stay tuned for an all-new Ally McBeal!

20:50.281 --> 20:54.578
Holy crap! Chris, that was amazing.
I mean, I just froze up.

20:54.578 --> 20:58.416
But you handled that bear like a real man.
I'm proud of you, son.

20:58.540 --> 21:03.215
You are? Because I heard
what you said about my huge... you know.

21:03.340 --> 21:06.677
Oh. Oh, you heard that, huh?

21:06.760 --> 21:11.681
I was just being stupid. Take it from me,
that thing you got there is a blessing.

21:11.764 --> 21:16.355
I mean, every guy you see with a big house
or a fancy car or a shiny gold tooth

21:16.481 --> 21:19.399
is really just saying
"Don't look at my penis. "

21:19.399 --> 21:24.280
- But you'll never have to worry about that.
- Thanks, Dad! You're the best.

21:25.239 --> 21:30.246
You know, Dad, I just realised something.
Your name's Peter.

21:31.163 --> 21:34.000
You're right, it is.

